hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1204","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""Tell me of an act of worship that is equal in reward to Jihad."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""I do not find any such act."" (Then) the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Can you do this: when a Mujahid goes out (for Jihad), you stand in your mosque (praying) without showing any laziness, and you keep fasting continuously without breaking it?"" He said, ""Who can do that?"""
"1205","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who is the best among all people?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""A believer who strives in the way of Allah with his life and his wealth."" The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked, ""Who after him?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""A believer who lives in a mountain pass, worshipping Allah and keeping people safe from his harm."""
"1206","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever fights in the way of Allah, and Allah knows best who fights in His way, his example is like that of a person who fasts continuously during the day and stands in prayer throughout the night. And Allah has taken it upon Himself that whoever fights in His way, if He causes him to die, He will admit him to Paradise (without reckoning), or He will return him safely with reward and spoils of war."""
"1207","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, performs prayer, and fasts in Ramadan, it is Allah’s promise to admit him into Paradise, whether he fights in the path of Allah or remains in the land where he was born.” The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said, “O Messenger of Allah! Should we not make this known among the people?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are one hundred levels in Paradise which Allah has prepared for those who fight in His path. The distance between each two levels is as great as that between the sky and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaus, for it is the best and highest part of Paradise.” I think the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also said (after this): “Above it (i.e., Jannat al-Firdaus) is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it flow the rivers of Paradise.”"
"1208","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""To go forth in the morning or evening in the way of Allah is better than the whole world and whatever is in it."""
"1209","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a small place in Paradise, even as much as a bow, is better than all the worldly things upon which the sun rises and sets."" And he (peace be upon him) said: ""To go out in the morning or evening in the way of Allah is better than all those things upon which the sun rises or sets."""
"1210","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If a woman (i.e., a Hoor) from among the people of Paradise were to look down upon the people of the earth, she would illuminate all the space between the heaven and the earth and fill it with fragrance, and indeed, the veil on her head is better than the entire world and whatever is in it."""
"1211","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sent some people from the tribe of Banu Sahm to the tribe of Banu Amir along with seventy men (as ambassadors). When they reached there, my maternal uncle (Haram bin Milhan) said to them, ""I will go first. If they grant me security so that I can convey to them the message of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), (that is better); otherwise, stay close to me (and help me at the right time)."" So he went ahead, and the disbelievers granted him security. While he was delivering the message of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to them, suddenly they signaled to one of their men, and he struck him with a spear and pierced him through. He said, ""Allahu Akbar! By the Lord of the Ka'bah! I have succeeded (in my purpose)."" After that, they turned towards his remaining companions and killed them, except for one lame man who climbed up a mountain and survived. Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) informed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that those people (who had been sent as ambassadors) had all met their Lord, and He is pleased with them, and they are pleased with Him. Then we used to recite this verse in the Qur'an: ""Convey to our people that we have met our Lord, and He is pleased with us, and has made us pleased."" After that, this verse was abrogated. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) invoked curses for forty days upon the people of Ril, Dhakwan, Banu Lihyan, and Banu Usayyah, who had disobeyed Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1212","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jundub bin Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was in a battle when his finger became wounded and bloodied. So the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""You are but a finger that has become bloodied, and this calamity you have borne is in the way of Allah."""
"1213","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, no person will be wounded in the way of Allah—and Allah knows well the one who is wounded in His way—but that he will come on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that the color of his blood will be like the color of blood, but its fragrance will be like the fragrance of musk."""
"1214","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` my uncle Anas bin Nadr (may Allah be pleased with him) did not participate in the Battle of Badr, so he submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! The very first battle that you (peace be upon him) fought against the polytheists, I was not present in it. Well, now if Allah gives me the opportunity to participate in any battle against the polytheists, then surely Allah will see what I do."" Then when the day of the Battle of Uhud came and the Muslims fled, he said, ""O Allah! I apologize for what the Muslims have done, and I disassociate myself from what the polytheists have done."" Then he advanced and met Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him). He said, ""O Sa'd! By the Lord of Nadr: 'Paradise is near. I am smelling the fragrance of Paradise from the other side of Uhud.'"" Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say, ""O Messenger of Allah! What Anas bin Nadr (may Allah be pleased with him) did, I could not do (even though I am also among the brave ones of Arabia)."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we found our uncle (in the battlefield) martyred, and there were more than eighty (80) wounds of swords, spears, and arrows on his body, and the polytheists had mutilated him (i.e., they had cut off his limbs, nose, ears, etc.), so except for his sister, no one recognized him. She recognized him by his fingers. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say that we think that this verse was revealed about him and such Muslims: ""Among the believers are men who have been true to their covenant with Allah..."" Then he says that his sister, whose name was Rubayyi', broke the front teeth of a woman, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) ordered retribution (qisas). Anas (bin Nadr, may Allah be pleased with him) submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! By Him Who has sent you with the truth, my sister's teeth will not be broken."" Then the claimants became satisfied with blood money and forgave the retribution, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, ""Among the servants of Allah are some who, if they swear by Allah relying on Him, Allah fulfills it for them."""
"1215","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say that when the Holy Qur’an was written in a Mushaf (codex) by copying from scattered parchments, I could not find the verse (23) of Surah Al-Ahzab. I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting it. Then I found it only with Khuzaymah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), whose testimony the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had considered equal to the testimony of two men. That verse was: “Among the believers are men who have been true to their covenant with Allah; some of them have fulfilled their vow (by being martyred)....”"
"1216","Narrated by Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him): A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) equipped with weapons and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Should I go for jihad or (first) accept Islam?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""First accept Islam, then go for jihad."" So he did so, and (in jihad) he was martyred. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""He did very little work but will receive a great reward."""
"1217","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): Umm Rabi', the daughter of Bara', who was the mother of Haritha bin Suraqa, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Tell me about Haritha."" He had been killed on the day of Badr, struck by an unknown arrow. She said, ""If he is in Paradise, I will be patient (knowing he is at ease), but if it is otherwise, then I will weep for him profusely."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Umm Haritha! (Not just one Paradise) There are many gardens (Paradises) within Paradise, and indeed your son is in the highest Paradise, Al-Firdaus."""
"1218","Narrated Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him): A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""Some people fight for war booty, some for fame, and some to show their bravery. So who is the one who fights in the way of Allah (fi sabilillah)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Only the one who fights so that the word of Allah becomes supreme is the one who is in the way of Allah (fi sabilillah)."""
"1219","Narrated by Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from (the battle of) Khandaq and had put down his weapons and taken a bath, Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to him and there was still dust on his head. Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ""You have put down your weapons, but I have not yet put mine down."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Where to now?"" Jibreel (peace be upon him) pointed towards Banu Qurayza and said, ""That way."" Umm al-Mu'minin (may Allah be pleased with her) says that then (immediately) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in that direction."
"1220","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah will smile at two men, one of whom killed the other, yet both will enter Paradise. One fought in the way of Allah and was martyred. Then Allah granted the killer the ability to repent (he became a Muslim), and he too was martyred (in the way of Allah)."""
"1221","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, he (peace be upon him) was in Khaybar. The Muslims had conquered Khaybar. I submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! (In the spoils of war) allot my share as well."" Then one of the sons of Sa'id bin 'As said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do not allot his share."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! He is the killer of Ibn Qawqal (may Allah be pleased with him)."" So the son of Sa'id bin 'As said, ""How strange! (Abu Hurairah) who has come to us from the direction of Dhan (the name of a mountain) accuses me of killing a Muslim, whom Allah honored at my hands (i.e., with martyrdom) and did not disgrace me at his hands (i.e., by being killed and becoming a wretched corpse of Hellfire)."""
"1222","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) did not observe (voluntary) fasts during the time of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) due to participating in jihad (so that his strength would not diminish). Then, when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, I never saw him leaving the fast except on the days of Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha."
"1223","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: ""The plague is a cause of martyrdom for every Muslim."""
"1224","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was having me write this verse: ""The believers who sit (at home) without any excuse are not equal to those who strive in the way of Allah with their lives and wealth."" Meanwhile, Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him) came and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! If I had the ability, I would certainly participate in jihad,"" and he was a blind man. Then Allah began to send revelation to His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him). At that time, the thigh of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was resting on my thigh, and due to the effect of the revelation, his thigh became so heavy that I feared my thigh would be crushed. After that, when that state was lifted from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Allah revealed: ""Except those who are excused."" (For example, the blind, the lame, the disabled, etc.)"
"1225","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went towards the trench (which was being dug around Madinah). He saw that the Muhajirun and Ansar were digging the trench early in the cold mornings. They did not have any slaves to do this work for them. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw their distress and hunger, he recited this verse: ""O Allah! The real goodness is the goodness of the Hereafter, so bestow Your blessings upon the Muhajirun and Ansar."" In response, the Muhajirun and Ansar said: ""We are those who have pledged allegiance to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the condition that we will continue to strive in Jihad as long as there is life in our bodies."""
"1226","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in one narration that (in the Battle of Khandaq, the Muhajirun and Ansar used to) say: ""We are those who pledged allegiance to Muhammad (peace be upon him) on the condition that as long as there is life in our bodies, we will continue to strive (in jihad)."" So the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) would reply to them: ""O Allah! True goodness is only the goodness of the Hereafter, so bless the Muhajirun and the Ansar."""
"1227","Narrated Al-Bara' bin 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him): I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Battle of Ahzab carrying earth, and the dust had covered the color of his stomach, and he was saying: ""O Allah! If it were not for You, we would not have been guided, nor would we have given charity, nor prayed. So send down tranquility upon us, and make our feet firm when we meet the enemy. Indeed, those people have rebelled against us. Whenever they intend mischief, we do not obey them."""
"1228","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): When we returned from the Battle of Tabuk with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Some people have remained behind in Madinah, but there is no mountain pass or valley which we crossed except that they were with us (in reward). They were held back by a (valid) excuse."""
"1229","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed, whoever fasts for one day in the way of Allah (i.e., in jihad), Allah will distance his face from the Hellfire by a distance of seventy years."""
"1230","Narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever equips a warrior in the way of Allah, it is as if he himself has fought, and whoever looks after the family of a warrior in the way of Allah in his absence, it is as if he himself has fought."""
"1231","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) in Madinah would not visit anyone’s house except that of Umm Sulaym and his noble wives. So someone asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) the reason for this, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “I feel compassion for her; her brother was martyred along with me.”"
"1232","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he went to Thabit bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) and he was applying perfume with both his thighs uncovered. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""O uncle! What is preventing you (from the battle)?"" He replied, ""O son of my brother! I am coming just now."" Then he continued applying perfume. Then he came and sat among the (fighters). Then it was told that in this battle the Muslims suffered a slight defeat, so Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the people, ""Move aside, give us space, we will fight the disbelievers. We did not do this in battle with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); rather, we used to stand firm and fight. You have given your enemies a bad habit (by fleeing)."""
"1233","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said during the Battle of Ahzab, ""Who will bring me news of the enemy?"" Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I will (bring it)."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again said, ""Who will bring me news of the enemy?"" He again said, ""I (will bring it)."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1234","Narrated from Sayyiduna Urwah al-Bariqi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Goodness and blessing are tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. (That is, either everlasting reward in the Hereafter or spoils of war in this world.)"""
"1235","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is goodness and blessing in the forelocks of horses."""
"1236","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a horse for fighting in the way of Allah, solely out of faith in Allah and believing in His promises, then surely its food, drink, dung, and urine—in short, everything related to it—will become reward for him and will be weighed in his scale of deeds on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1237","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) says that there was a horse of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept in our garden; its name was Laheef, and some say its name was Lakheef."
"1238","‘Sayyiduna Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a donkey, whose name was ‘Ufair. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “O Mu’adh! Do you know what Allah’s right is upon His servants?” ... and the entire hadith was narrated which has already passed. (See the Book: Statement of Knowledge... Chapter: Disliking that people may not understand, for the one who leaves one group for another to teach them knowledge.)"
"1239","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that (once) there was some fear in Madinah, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted our horse whose name was Mandub. He (peace be upon him) went out. When he returned, he said: ""We did not see anything to be afraid of, and indeed we found this horse to be swift like a river."""
"1240","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Omen is only in three things: (1) the horse, (2) the woman, (3) the house."""
"1241","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted two shares for the horse and one share for its rider (in the spoils of war)."
"1242","A person asked Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Did you people run away leaving the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the Battle of Hunayn?"" He replied, ""(Yes), but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not run away. (The reason was that the tribe of) Hawazin (were) great archers. When we confronted them and attacked them, they fled. Then the Muslims turned towards the spoils of war, and the disbelievers started showering arrows (so we retreated), but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not run away. Indeed, I saw him riding his white mule, and Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) was holding its reins, and the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was saying, 'I am a Prophet, there is no lie in this. I am the son of Abdul Muttalib (the chief).' """
"1243","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the she-camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whose name was Adhba, no other she-camel could surpass her. Then a Bedouin youth came riding a camel and he surpassed her, which was very hard on the Muslims, until when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know of it, he said: ""It is Allah's right that whatever is elevated in the world, He will also bring it low."""
"1244","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he distributed some sheets among the women of Madinah, and a very fine sheet was left. One of those sitting with him said, ""O Commander of the Faithful! Give this sheet to the granddaughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who is in your wedlock."" They meant Umm Kulthum bint Ali. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Umm Sulayt (may Allah be pleased with her) is more deserving of it. She was an Ansari woman. She had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""On the day of Uhud, she used to bring water skins filled with water for us."""
"1245","Lady Ruba'i bint Mu'awwidh (may Allah be pleased with her) says: We used to accompany the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) (in jihad), and we would give water (to the fighters), treat the wounded, and carry the martyrs and the injured back to Madinah."
"1246","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not sleep one night during a journey, so when he reached Madinah, (he was overcome by sleep). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “If only one of my righteous companions would guard me tonight.” Suddenly, we heard the sound of a weapon. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Who is it?” He replied, “Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas. I have come to guard you, O Messenger of Allah.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) slept."
"1247","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “May the slave of the dirham, the dinar, and the cloak be destroyed; if he is given, he is pleased, and if he is not given, he is displeased. (Such a person) is destroyed and thrown down, and if a thorn pricks him, may no one remove it. Glad tidings to that servant who keeps the reins of his horse in his hand at all times for striving in the way of Allah; his head is covered with dust, his feet are covered with dust; if he is told to stand guard, he stands guard, and if he is appointed at the rear of the army for protection, he remains at the rear. (In short, he obeys whatever order he is given, and due to his poverty, he has no status among the people of the world, to the extent that) if he seeks permission (to visit someone), he is not granted permission, and if he intercedes (for someone), his intercession is not accepted.”"
"1248","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): I went to Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to serve him. Then, when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was returning from Khaybar and Uhud mountain became visible to him, he said: ""This is a mountain that loves us and we love it."""
"1249","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): We were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The person who had the most shade among us was the one who had made shade with his cloak. Those who were fasting did not do any work, and those who were not fasting lifted up the water skins, filled them with water, and did all kinds of service and work. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Today, those who did not fast have taken all the reward."""
"1250","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Guarding for one day in the way of Allah is better than the whole world and whatever is in it. And your smallest place in Paradise, even if it is as small as a whip, is better than the whole world and whatever is in it. And the servant who walks in the way of Allah in the morning or evening, that is better than the whole world and whatever is in it.”"
"1251","It is narrated from the conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), that he thought he had superiority over many other companions (because of his wealth and bravery). So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are helped and provided for because of your weak ones."""
"1252","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A time will come when people will wage jihad, and it will be said: 'Is there anyone among you who has accompanied the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?' It will be answered: 'Yes, there is.' (Supplication will be made through them) and victory will be granted. Then a time will come when people will say: 'Is there anyone among you who has accompanied the companions of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?' It will be answered: 'Yes, there is.' (Then supplication will be made through them and) victory will be granted. Then a time will come when it will be said: 'Is there anyone among you who has accompanied the one who accompanied the companions of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?' It will be answered: 'Yes, there is.' (Then supplication will be made through them and) victory will be granted."""
"1253","Sayyiduna Abu Usaid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr, when we had formed rows against the Quraysh and they had formed rows against us, said: ""When they come close to you, then shoot arrows at them."""
"1254","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the wealth of Banu Nadir was of the type which Allah granted to His Messenger (peace be upon him) without battle. The Muslims had not made their horses or riders run upon it, meaning there was no occasion of war. So that wealth was taken especially by the Prophet (peace be upon him), and from it he would give his family their expenses for one year. After a year, whatever remained, he would spend it on weapons, horses, and for striving in the path of Allah."
"1255","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I did not see the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say for anyone except Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) that his parents be sacrificed for him. (In the Battle of Uhud) I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Shoot, Sa'd! May my parents be sacrificed for you."""
"1256","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""Indeed, all these conquests were achieved by those whose swords had neither gold nor silver work on them. Their swords had work of leather, lead, and iron."""
"1257","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` on the day of Badr, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was inside a tent, he said: ""O Allah! I beseech You by Your covenant and Your promise (to grant victory to the Muslims). O Allah! If You will, after today You will never be worshipped (on earth again)."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) took hold of his (the Prophet's) hand and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! (This much supplication) is sufficient for you. Indeed, you have reached the limit in supplicating to your Lord."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wearing armor at that time. Then he (peace be upon him) came out saying these words: ""Soon this group will be defeated and they will turn their backs and flee. Rather, the Hour is their appointed time, and the Hour is more grievous and bitter."" (Surah Al-Qamar 45, 46) And in another narration, it is mentioned that this incident took place on the day of Badr."
"1258","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) to wear silk shirts because they had itching on their bodies."
"1259","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman and Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them) complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lice, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them to wear silk garments."
"1260","Narrated by Umm Haram (may Allah be pleased with her): She heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""The first people among my Ummah who will fight in the sea, Paradise will be obligatory for them."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Am I among them?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""You are among them."" Umm Haram (may Allah be pleased with her) says that then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""The first people among my Ummah who will fight in the city of Caesar (Constantinople), they will be forgiven."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Am I among those people?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""No (you are not among them)."""
"1261","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""You will fight the Jews until a Jew will hide behind a stone, and the stone will say: O servant of Allah (Muslim)! There is a Jew hiding behind me. Kill him."" In another narration, it is said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight the Jews..."" Then the rest of the hadith was narrated."
"1262","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight the Turks, whose eyes are small, faces are red, and noses are wide and flat. Their faces will be like shields covered with leather. And the Hour will not be established until you fight a people who wear shoes made of hair."""
"1263","Narrated Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked against the polytheists on the day of the Battle of the Trench, saying: ""O Allah! Revealer of the Book! Swift in reckoning! O Allah! Defeat these groups, shake their feet, scatter them (O Allah! Scatter them and destroy them, scatter them, make them stumble)."""
"1264","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Jews (one day) came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and said, ""Death be upon you."" So I cursed them. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""What happened to you?"" I said, ""Did you not hear what they said?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Did you not hear what I replied? I said, 'And upon you' (meaning, whatever you have said is upon you)."""
"1265","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): Tufail bin Amr Dausi and his companions (may Allah be pleased with them) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The people of the tribe of Daus have disobeyed and refused to follow, so pray to Allah against them."" The people said, ""Now Daus is destroyed,"" but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed: ""O Allah! Guide Daus and bring them to Islam."""
"1266","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Khaybar: “I will give the flag to that person by whose hand victory will be granted.” So the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) stood up hoping that the flag would be given to one of them. Then the next day, every person hoped that the flag would be given to them, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Where is Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)?” Someone informed that he has pain in both his eyes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he be called. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied his saliva to both his eyes, and he was immediately cured (it seemed as if) he had no ailment at all. Then he asked whether we should fight these disbelievers until they become Muslim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Proceed gently. When you reach their field, invite them to Islam and inform them of what is obligatory upon them from Allah. By Allah! If even one person is guided through you, it is better for you than red camels.”"
"1267","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that it was rare for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to set out on a journey on any day other than Thursday."
"1268","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in a military expedition and said to us: ""If you find so-and-so and so-and-so (he mentioned the names of two men from the Quraysh), then burn them with fire."" Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then when we were about to depart on the journey, we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to bid him farewell, and he said: ""I had ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so with fire, but none punishes with fire except Allah. Therefore, if you capture them, kill them."""
"1269","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Listening to and obeying (the Imam's command) is obligatory upon everyone, as long as it is not against the Shari'ah. But if one is ordered to commit a sin, then neither listening nor obeying is necessary."""
"1270","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""We are the last among the nations in terms of time, but the foremost in rank."" And he said: ""Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. And whoever obeys the (lawful) leader has indeed obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the (lawful) leader has indeed disobeyed me. And the Imam is like a shield; fighting is done from behind him, and he is a means of protection. So if he commands the fear of Allah and acts justly, then he will be rewarded for that, and if he does otherwise, then he will bear the sin for that."""
"1271","´Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that (after the Pledge of Ridwan) when we came again the following year, not even two men among us could agree on identifying the tree under which we had pledged (Ridwan). (There was some mercy from Allah in this.) It was asked: On what matter was the pledge taken from the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them all), was it on death? He replied: No, rather the pledge was taken on patience."
"1272","Abdullah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the incident of Harrah occurred, a person came to him and said, ""The son of Hanzalah is taking allegiance from people on the condition of death."" So Abdullah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""After the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we will not pledge allegiance to anyone on this condition (i.e., on the condition of death)."""
"1273","Narrated Salama bin Al-Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him): I gave the pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (at the event of the Pledge of Ridwan). After that, I went towards the shade of a tree. When the crowd of people lessened, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Ibn Akwa’! Will you not give the pledge?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have already given the pledge.” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Even so (do it again).” So I gave the pledge to him again. It was asked, “Abu Muslim (this is the kunyah of Salama bin Al-Akwa’), on what did you pledge allegiance that day?” He said: “On death.”"
"1274","Narrated Sayyiduna Mujashi’ (may Allah be pleased with him): I brought my brother’s son to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “Please take the pledge of allegiance from him for migration.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, “Migration has ended for its people.” I asked, “Then on what will you take the pledge from us?” He replied, “On Islam and Jihad.”"
"1275","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said one day that` today a person came to me and asked me a question. I did not understand what answer to give him. He said, tell me about a person who is heavily armed, perfectly healthy, he goes out in jihads with our leaders, then he gives us such commands in some matters that we cannot carry them out. I said to him, by Allah, I do not understand what answer to give you except that when we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would command us in every matter only once until we would carry it out, and indeed every one of you will remain on goodness as long as he fears Allah, and when any doubt arises in his heart about something, he should ask someone, and he will satisfy him, and soon you will not find such a person (whose decision brings satisfaction). By the One besides whom there is no deity, as much of the world has passed (and as much remains), I say about it that the world is like a pond whose clear water has been drunk and only the muddy water remains."
"1276","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, on some occasions during jihad, in which there was confrontation with the enemy, delayed the battle. When the sun had declined, he stood up and delivered a sermon and said: ""O people! Do not wish to meet the enemy and ask Allah for well-being. But when you do confront the enemy, then be patient and know well that Paradise is under the shade of swords."" After this he said: ""O Allah! Revealer of the Book (Qur'an), Mover of the clouds, and Defeater of the confederates! Defeat them and grant us victory over them."""
"1277","Sayyiduna Ya'la bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I had hired a man, and he fought with another man. One of them bit the other's hand with his mouth. The other pulled his hand out of his mouth, and his front teeth fell out. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not award him compensation for the teeth and said: ""Would he have left his hand in your mouth so that you could chew it, just as a camel chews greenery?"""
"1278","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said to Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded you to plant the flag at this place."
"1279","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have been sent with concise speech and I have been supported through awe. So (one day) while I was sleeping, the keys to all the treasures of the earth were brought and placed in my hand."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) (after narrating this hadith) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has departed (from this world) and now you are extracting those treasures."
"1280","Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the house of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) when he intended to migrate to Madinah. She says: I could not find anything with which I could tie the food and the water container for him, so I said to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): By Allah! I do not find anything except my waistband with which I can tie them. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Divide your waistband into two parts, tie the water container with one and the food with the other. So I did so, and for this reason I was named ""the possessor of two waistbands"" (Dhat an-Nitaqain)."
"1281","Narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode on a donkey on whose saddle there was a sheet, and he seated Sayyiduna Usama (may Allah be pleased with him) behind him."
"1282","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah came riding on a camel from the higher part of Makkah, with Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) seated behind him. With him was Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and with him was Uthman bin Talha (who was among the custodians of the Ka'bah), until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made the camel sit in the mosque. Then he ordered Uthman to bring the key of the Ka'bah, so the Ka'bah was opened and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered it... The rest of the hadith has already been mentioned. (See the Book: Description of Prayer... Chapter: Praying between the pillars without congregation)"
"1283","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade traveling with the Noble Qur'an to the land of the enemy."
"1284","´Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during Hajj. When we would ascend a height, we would say La ilaha illallah and Allahu Akbar. Our voices would become loud, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Do not exert yourselves so much, make it easy upon yourselves, for you are not calling upon one who is deaf or absent. Indeed, He hears, He is near."" (One should also say Allahu Akbar while ascending stairs.)"
"1285","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): When we ascended to higher ground, we would say ""Allahu Akbar"" (Allah is the Greatest), and when we descended to lower ground, we would say ""Subhan Allah"" (Glory be to Allah). (When descending stairs, say Subhan Allah.)"
"1286","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant becomes ill or travels, whatever worship he used to perform while at home or in a state of health, all of that is written for him (i.e., there is no decrease in reward)."""
"1287","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""If people knew what harm there is in solitude, then no traveler would travel alone at night."""
"1288","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and asked his permission to participate in Jihad. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Are your parents alive?"" He replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Then strive in their service."" (Because they were old and helpless.)"
"1289","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bashir Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the people were in their sleeping places. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a messenger that nothing, whether a string or anything else, should remain on the neck of any camel except that it be cut off."
"1290","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""No man should sit in seclusion with a woman, and no woman should travel except with a mahram (close male relative)."" Then a man stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My name has been registered for such-and-such battle, and my wife is going for Hajj."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go and perform Hajj with your wife."""
"1291","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Allah is amazed at those people who are brought to Paradise in chains. (That is, they become Muslims)."""
"1292","Narrated Sa‘b bin Jaththamah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me at the place of Abwa’ or Waddan, and he was asked about the polytheists of Dar al-Harb, whether night raids could be carried out against them, and their women and children might also be killed. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They are from among them."" (If they are killed, there is no harm.) And I also heard him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Pasture lands are not permissible for anyone except Allah and His Messenger."""
"1293","Narrated by Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): In one of the battles of the Prophet (peace be upon him), a woman was found killed. The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade the killing of women and children."
"1294","When the news reached Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Commander of the Faithful, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), had burned some people with fire, he said: If I were (the caliph), I would never have burned them. Because the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not punish anyone with Allah's punishment."" And indeed, I would have killed them as the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever changes his religion, kill him."""
"1295","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""An ant bit one of the Prophets from among the Prophets, so he ordered and the ant colony was burned. Then Allah revealed to him: 'An ant bit you, yet you burned a whole community that glorified Allah.'"""
"1296","Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that (one day) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Why do you not relieve me by destroying Dhu al-Khalasah?"" Dhu al-Khalasah was an idol-house among the tribe of Khath'am. It was called the Ka'bah of Yemen. Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that then I set out with one hundred and fifty horsemen from the tribe of Ahmas, and all of them had horses, but my feet would not stay firm on the horse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his hand on my chest until I saw the mark of his fingers on my chest, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed: ""O Allah! Keep them firm, and make them guided and guiding."" So they went there and destroyed it and burned it. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of this, the messenger of Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) came and reported to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""By the One Who sent you with the truth, I have come to you at a time when I left it in a state like a hollow camel or a mangy camel."" Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for blessing for the horses and horsemen of the tribe of Ahmas five times."
"1297","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Kisra has perished, and there will be no Kisra after him, and Caesar will also perish, and there will be no Caesar after him, and surely you will distribute the treasures of Caesar and Kisra in the way of Allah."""
"1298","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called war a deception."
"1299","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that on the day of Uhud, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Abdullah bin Jubair (may Allah be pleased with him) as the leader of the foot soldiers (and they were fifty men), and said: “If you see us in such a state that birds are eating our flesh (i.e., we are defeated and killed), even then do not leave your position until I call you back. And if you see that we have defeated the disbelievers and trampled them, even then do not move until I call you back.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) defeated the disbelievers. Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: By Allah, I saw the women running, lifting their clothes, exposing their anklets and shins. Then those with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O people! The spoils of war, the spoils of war! Your companions have prevailed, what are you waiting for now? Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Have you forgotten the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: By Allah, we will go to the people and collect the spoils of war. So when they went there and turned away, the disbelievers came running and the battle resumed. Thus, only twelve men remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The disbelievers martyred seventy of our men, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) had inflicted losses on one hundred and forty polytheists on the day of Badr: seventy prisoners and seventy killed. Abu Sufyan said three times: Is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alive among the people? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade answering. After that, Abu Sufyan said three times: Is the son of Abu Quhafah (Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him) alive among the people? Then he said: Is the son of Khattab (Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) alive among the people? He said this three times. Then he turned to his companions and said: These people have been killed. So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) could not restrain himself and said: By Allah, O enemy of Allah! Those whom you have named are all alive, and your bad day is yet to come. Abu Sufyan said: Today is revenge for the day of Badr, and battle is like a bucket (sometimes up, sometimes down), and you will find mutilation among the people, but I neither ordered it nor did I dislike it. After that, Abu Sufyan began to chant: “O Hubal! Be exalted, O Hubal! Be exalted.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Why do you not answer him?” The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: O Messenger of Allah! What should we say? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: “Allah is the highest and most majestic.” Then Abu Sufyan said: We have Uzza, and you have no Uzza. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Why do you not answer him?” The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: O Messenger of Allah! What should we say? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: “Allah is our Protector, and you have no protector.”"
"1300","Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was going from Madinah towards Ghabah. When I reached the hill of Ghabah, I met a slave of Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him). I said, “Hey! How are you here?” He said that the camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have been seized (I am searching for them). I asked, “Who has seized them?” The slave said, “Ghatafan and Fazarah.” Then I shouted so loudly three times that the whole of Madinah heard me: “Ya Sabahah! Ya Sabahah!” After that, I ran and caught up with the robbers, and they were taking away the camels. So I started shooting arrows at them and kept saying: “I am Salamah bin Akwa’, know this... Today all the wicked will die, accept it...” Thus, I rescued the camels from them before they could drink their milk. Then, as I was driving them back, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me. I submitted, “O Messenger of Allah! Those people were thirsty, and before they could drink the milk, I quickly took these camels away. So please send an army in their pursuit.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O son of Akwa’! You have already overpowered them, now let them go (forgive them). They have reached their people, and there they will be entertained.”"
"1301","Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Free the captive, feed the hungry, and visit the sick."" (And it is obligatory to free a Muslim captive by whatever means possible.)"
"1302","Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I asked Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Do you have any revelation besides the Book of Allah?"" He said, ""No, by Him who split the grain (and brought forth the tree from it) and created the soul: I do not know of anything else, except for an understanding that Allah gives to a person in (understanding) the meanings of the Qur'an, and whatever is in this scroll."" I asked, ""What is in this scroll?"" He said, ""It is about blood money (diyah), the responsibility of the 'aqilah (the male relatives who pay blood money), the freeing of captives, and that no Muslim should be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever."""
"1303","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` some people from the Ansar sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), saying, ""O Messenger of Allah! Allow us to waive the ransom of our nephew, Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him)."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not leave even a single dirham from him."""
"1304","Saidna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a spy from the polytheists came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he (the Prophet) was on a journey. He (the spy) sat with the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and started talking. After that, he left, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Catch him and kill him.” And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his belongings to the one who killed him."
"1305","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""The day of Thursday, oh the day of Thursday."" Then he began to weep, and wept so much that the pebbles of the ground became wet. Then he said: ""On Thursday, the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intensified, so he said: 'Bring me something to write with, so that I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.' But the people differed, although it is not appropriate to differ in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the people said that (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is) talking deliriously due to the severity of his illness. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Leave me, for the state I am in is better than what you are calling me to.' And at the time of his death, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made three bequests: (1) That the polytheists should be expelled from the Arabian Peninsula; (2) and that ambassadors should be treated as I used to treat them; and the third matter, I forgot."""
"1306","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people and praised Allah as He deserves to be praised. Then he mentioned the Dajjal and said: ""I warn you against the Dajjal, and every prophet has warned his people against the Dajjal, but I will tell you something which no prophet has told his people. Know that he will be one-eyed, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed."" (The complete hadith has already been mentioned in the Book of Funerals... Chapter: If a child accepted Islam and then died, should the funeral prayer be offered for him and can the invitation to Islam be presented to a child? This part is not included there, so read both together.)"
"1307","Narrated by Sayyiduna Hudhaifah bin Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him): (On one occasion) the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Write down the names of all those who recite the Kalimah of Islam and bring them before me."" So we wrote down the names of one thousand five hundred men. Then we thought to ourselves, should we still fear the disbelievers when we are one thousand five hundred men? But indeed, we found ourselves overcome by fear, to the extent that a man would pray alone out of fear."
"1308","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevailed over any people, he would stay in that field for three days."
"1309","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that one of his horses ran away. The enemy captured it and took it away. Then, when the Muslims prevailed over the disbelievers, the horse was returned to Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And one of his slaves (also) ran away. He joined the Romans (disbelievers). When the Muslims prevailed over them, Khalid bin Walid (may Allah be pleased with him), after the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), returned that slave to Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"1310","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): I once said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We have slaughtered a small goat and ground a sa’ of barley flour, so please come with a few of your companions (may Allah be pleased with them)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then called out loudly, ""O people of the Trench! Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) has prepared some food for you, so come quickly."" (The word ""Suran"" is Persian; the chapter heading is derived from here.)"
"1311","Lady Umm Khalid bint Khalid bin Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I went with my father to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at that time I was wearing a yellow (colored) shirt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sanah."" And this is a word in the Abyssinian language, which means ""good"" (i.e., it is good). Umm Khalid (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Then I began to play with the seal of Prophethood, so my father scolded me, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave her."" After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (prayed for my long life, that is) said: ""Wear it out and tear it, then wear it out and tear it, then wear it out and tear it."""
"1312","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): (One day) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us, then he mentioned the matter of embezzlement from war booty and declared it to be a grave (serious sin), and he made its matter very severe. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I should not find any one of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that a goat is mounted on his neck and it is bleating, (or) a horse is mounted on his neck and it is neighing. (Then this person) will say: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I have no authority for you, I had conveyed (the message of Allah) to you. And a camel is mounted on his neck and it is grunting, and he will say: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I have no authority for you, I had conveyed (the message of Allah) to you. And (gold, silver, goods) are loaded on his neck and he says to me: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, but I will say to him: I cannot help you in any way, or I had conveyed the message to you. Or there are clothes on his neck which are fluttering, and he says: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, so I will say: I have no authority for you, I had conveyed (the message of Allah) to you."""
"1313","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them) that: There was a man assigned to the belongings of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his name was ""Karkarah"". Then he died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He is in Hell."" Then people began to look into his condition, and they found a cloak (sheet) among his possessions from the war booty, which he had taken deceitfully."
"1314","Sayyiduna Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Ibn Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Do you remember when we, you, and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) went to welcome the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" He said, ""Yes (I remember)."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made us ride with him (on his mount) and did not make you ride."
"1315","Sayyiduna Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we used to go with the boys up to Thaniyyatul Wada’ to welcome the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1316","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we were with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) while returning from Usfan, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was riding his camel, and Umm al-Mu'mineen Safiyyah bint Huyayy (may Allah be pleased with her) was seated behind him. Then the foot of the Prophet's (peace and blessings be upon him) camel slipped, and both of them fell down. So Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) quickly jumped down (from his camel) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! May Allah sacrifice me for you (did you get hurt)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Take care of the woman."" So Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) covered his face with a cloth and went to Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her), covered her with a sheet, and set the mount right. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Umm al-Mu'mineen Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) mounted, and we surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). After that, when we approached Madinah, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""We are returning, if Allah wills, repentant, worshipping, and praising our Lord."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) kept saying this until we reached Madinah."
"1317","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ka'b (bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would return from a journey at the time of forenoon, he would go to the mosque and perform two units of prayer before sitting down."
